      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "L'Anse Township was established on May 8, 1846, but the rich history of the area began many years before.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lansetownship.org/home-1/township-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Village of L'Anse came into existence in 1871 because of a new railroad line and terminus that ended at the head of Keweenaw Bay.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lansetownship.org/home-1/township-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1896, the village was completely burned to the ground by a deadly fire which left many homeless.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L'Anse%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "L'Anse Township history would not be complete without mentioning the founder of Ford Motor Company, Henry Ford.",
